  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "All green sulfur bacteria were grown in Pfennig’s medium (Pfennig and Trüper 1992)"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Cultures were grown anaerobically in the light using 100-ml screw-capped bottles and incubated at 20 °C."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "When the autoclaved solution I (including solution 2) is cold, the following sterile solutions 3 through 5 are aseptically added while magnetically stirring the medium:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "After additions from solutions 1 through 5, the pH of the medium is adjusted with sterile 2M H2SO4 or Na2CO3 solution to pH 7.3 for purple sulfur bacteria or to pH 6.8 for green sulfur bacteria."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "For marine strains, add 20 g NaCI to solution 1 and increase the MgSO4.7H2O to 3 g."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "The solution is autoclaved in the cotton-plugged, 2-liter Erlenmeyer flask."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "The salts are dissolved in the order given and the solution is autoclaved in a screw-cap bottle."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 16,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": "The 5% solution is prepared in distilled water and is filter-sterilized."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 19,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 21,
      "comment": "A freshly autoclaved 6% solution is prepared in distilled water."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 22,
      "comment": "6 ml is added to medium for purple sulfur bacteria, or 10 ml to medium for green sulfur bacteria."
    }
  ]
}